> there's a little less worry that their artful wishes will be blocked.

Wizards can wish for Magicbane just as easily as any other class.

There will be no less worry on other classes' part, as it was already
trivial to avoid sacrificing at altars until you wished up your
artifacts of choice; this change does not reduce the possibility of
random objects being generated as artifacts on level creation.

Also, this change does not target Magicbane; it is targeting the problem of
artifact weapons in general being available too early in the game, rendering
95% of 'ordinary' weapons meaningless.

This also allows for stronger 'ordinary' artifacts that can be geared more
towards the environment a higher-level character will be facing, to make
a wider variety of artifacts desirable in the late game.

